{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1428557-tc-adventure-\u2014-prototype-edition","id":1428557,"title":"TC:Adventure! \u2014 prototype edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-15T21:40:00-08:00","id":1428557,"title":"TC:Adventure! \u2014 prototype edition","content":"This thread is intended to put together a workable model of what <b>TC: Adventure!</b> <i>could</i> be like (but probably won't), so that owners of the original <b>Adventure!</b> and of <b>Trinity Continuum</b> can run games in the original setting (or a close approximation of it) while waiting for the official <b>TC:A!</b> to come out. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">[As of this edit, TC:A! is being crowdfunded; so I'm reporting this as a system hack for TC:A!.]</span><br /> <br /> I'll be focusing mainly on the rules, as the setting is mostly fine as is; and the main tweaks are things like Sara Kaur's inclusion in the Hammersmith Event, things which have already been addressed in <b>TC:\u00c6</b>'s <i>The Secret History of Humanity</i> section. Seven in terms of the rules, most of what's needed is already in the <b>TC</b> core book. All that needs to be covered, really, are the rules for Mesmerists and Stalwarts. <br /> <br /> For the purpose of this hack, I'm going to treat Mesmerists and Stalwarts as variations on Talents (or Daredevils, as they're known in this era). I won't be doing things <i>precisely</i> the same way that <b>Adventure!</b> did them; but I'll be staying close enough that changes will mostly take the form of \u201cerrata\u201d rather than rewrites: you will need both <b>Trinity Continuum</b> and <b>Adventure!</b> to use this material. <br /> <br /> With that in mind, here we go: <br /> <b><u>Skills</u></b><br /> The Abilities in <b>Adventure!</b> don't match the Skills in <b>Trinity Continuum</b>; use the closest match. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">To do: Match <b>Adventure!</b>'s Abilities to <b>TC</b>'s Skills</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><b><u>Mesmerists</u></b><br /> Mesmerists differ from Talents in a few ways. First, their form of Inspiration has a different set of three Facets: <i>Biological</i>, <i>Energetic</i>, and <i>Cognitive</i>. <br /> <br /> Dots in Biological help the mesmerist get in tune with the living things around her; dots in Energetic help him deal with actions involving mechanics, kinetics, or energy; and dots in Cognitive help him deal with actions involving communication and perception. In all cases, you can spend a point of Inspiration to gain an Enhancement to your dice pool if it falls in the appropriate purview. These replace the Destructive Action, Intuitive Action, and Reflective Action uses of Inspiration on TC p.15. <br /> <br /> Mesmerists also replace Dramatic Editing with Attunement, which works much like its namesake in <b>TC:\u00c6on</b> (p.204): take an ordinary action and roll your highest Facet to pick up on Psychic or Dynamic Gifts or Powered Super-science being used nearby. You can forgo the roll by spending a point of Inspiration.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">[TC:A! instead goes with mesmerist-specific Dramatic Editing letting you replace your Psychic Gifts with other ones for a scene. Take your pick; or do both.]</span><br /> <br /> Psychic Gifts work like the Psychic Knacks in <b>Adventure!</b> (pp.162\u2013170), save for a change in the Facets. Change any references in a Psychic Knack's description to the following Mesmerist Facet: <br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Biological</b>: Brainstorm, Cloak of Dread, Evil Eye, Hypnotic Presence, Inspirational Aura, Psychic Control, Touch of Life<br /> \u2022 <b>Energetic</b>: Psychic Hand, Thermal Manipulation, Flame/Frost Conjuration, Teledigitation, Mindhammer, Sleight of Will<br /> \u2022 <b>Cognitive</b>: Brain Skimming, Command Voice, Marked Man, Perfect Translation, Scientific Prodigy, Telluric Resonance, Brainstorm, Hypnotic Presence, Cloud the Mind, Psychic Control, Psychic Synergy<br /> <br /> If a given Knack is listed under two Facets, take your choice. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">[I pulled the associations from <b>d20 Adventure!</b>, which listed Psi Aptitudes for each Psychic Knack. Biokinesis and Vitakinesis went to Biological; EK, PK, and Teleport went to Energetic; Clairvoyance and Telepathy went to Cognitive.]</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><b><u>Stalwarts</u></b><br /> The Facets of a Stalwart's Inspiration correspond to the three Approaches: <i>Forceful</i>, <i>Adaptive</i>, and <i>Stoic</i>. As with Mesmerists, Stalwarts replace the Destructive Action, Intuitive Action, and Reflective Action uses of Inspiration with ones aligning with their own Facets. <br /> <br /> <s>Stalwarts replace Dramatic Editing with an expanded version of Extraordinary Effort: for any action, spend a point of Inspiration to boost one type of Scale appropriate to it by an amount determined by the most suitable Facet: one dot in the Facet gives +1 Scale, three dots give +2 Scale, and five dots give +3 Scale.</s><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">[TC:A! has its own replacement for Dramatic Editing, which involves spending Inspiration to max out one or more Facets. It handles Scale benefits through Dynamic Gifts. As such, my patch above doesn't work.]</span><br /> <br /> Dynamic Gifts work just like their Dynamic Knack namesakes. As with Psychic Gifts, replace references to Destructive, Intuitive, and Reflective Facets with the most appropriate Stalwart Facet: <br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Physical</b>: A Single Bound, Cool Hand, Man for All Seasons, Powerlifter, Superhuman Reflexes, Blazing Speed, Optimized Metabolism, Piledriver, Body of Bronze, Reptilian Regeneration<br /> \u2022 <b>Mental</b>: Heightened Senses, Mad Scientist, Aetheric Vision, Blindfighter, Sun Tzu's Blessing, Indisputable Analysis, Sensory Filtering, Threat Awareness<br /> \u2022 <b>Social</b>: Sex Symbol, Touch of the Muses, Man of Many Faces<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">[Originally, I had the Facets organized by the Arenas. TC:A! went with the Approached instead (though not as Facets), so I'm following suit. As such, I need to revise these lists according to the Forceful/Adaptive/Stoic divide.]</span><br /> <br /> As an alternative, replace the Dynamic Knacks with a subset of the Superior Powers from <b>\u00c6on \u00c6xpansion</b>. Most of them work fine as is, as long as you're okay with none being written to make use of Facets and none of them costing Inspiration to use. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> I've debated repurposing the Daredevil, Stalwart, and Mesmerist names. Instead of being general-purpose terms referring to the three types of Inspired, I'm thinking of using them as informal nicknames for characters who are exceptionally strong in one Facet. For example: <br /> <br /> \u2022 <i>Talents</i>: Daredevils are the Intuitive ones; Masters are the Reflective ones; and Paragons are the Destructive ones. <br /> \u2022 <i>Psychics</i>: Healers instead of Biological; Kinetics instead of Energetic; Mesmerists instead of Cognitive<br /> \u2022 <i>___</i>: ___ instead of Forceful; ___ instead of Adaptive; Stalwart instead of Stoic","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-19-2021, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T04:37:35-08:00","id":1428585,"title":"","content":"Great ideas! Really, just awesome. The name ideas are a great idea for itself too.<br /> <br /> For those that don\u2019t have Adventure 1e, or are just lazy and don\u2019t what to convert the knacks:<br /> <br /> Paragons use Superior Powers from Aexpansion (just easy like that). Maybe the idea for relating it to the facets you can\u2019t buy a higher dot cost than the related facet. For inspiration cost, maybe 1 point to activate a power for 1 scene.<br /> <br /> Psychics use the powers from the modes related to their facets with a few twists:<br /> - The base powers becomes the 1st dot in the related modes.<br /> - You can pick any of the 2 base powers when you want to pick your first mode of that aptitude.<br /> - You pick the second base power when you want to pick your second mode of that aptitude.<br /> - The third mode have no base power, but you still need to spend one dot on that.<br /> - Ther first dot in the modes become the second dot in the knack, the second dot become the third dot in the knack and the third becomes the forth (and last) dot.<br /> <br /> For example: you want to learn Telekinesis, first dot you pick is any of the PK base powers (in this case Nudge seams a interesting option), second dot grants you Tow, third dot grants you Remote Hands and the 4th grants Velocity. If you wha to learn Perikinesis later, the first dot grants you Distant Touch, the second Kinetic Shield and so on. If you want to learn Thermo, there is no 1 dot power, but you get the second dot grants Equilibrium, and so on.<br /> <br /> Your Psi + Mode rolls become Facet + Knack. For base powers you pick your highest related knack to roll, even if not the one you used to learn.<br /> <br /> Notice that it allow some good use of powers, but as you have only Inspiration points, and not the pool Psi grants, the number of uses you have is lower (from 10 to 4) and the recovering is 1 point per scene, not a bunch after 5 minutes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 12-16-2020, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T07:08:04-08:00","id":1428595,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m confused. I thought Mesmerists were psiads, Stalwarts were low-powered novas and Daredevils were Talents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T07:18:38-08:00","id":1428598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1428557-tc-adventure-\u2014-prototype-edition?p=1428595#post1428595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m confused. I thought Mesmerists were psiads, Stalwarts were low-powered novas and Daredevils were Talents.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a yes and no kind of thing. You're not wrong, but they're also not fully those either. It was meant to be a little ambiguous. I don't know if it will still be that way in the new Adventure!. But in the old, the three types of &quot;Inspired&quot; are closer to each other than the types they resemble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T08:24:41-07:00","id":1444665,"title":"","content":"I've updated this in response to developments in the TC:A! Kickstarter. The biggest change is to replace Physical/Mental/Social with Forceful/Adaptive/Stoic; but I also renamed the Psychic Facets, and made a couple other small changes. <br /> <br /> TC:A! also introduces the notion that each type of Inspired has a Facet-specific means of generating Inspiration (daredevils use Intuitive, mesmerists use Reflective, and stalwarts use Destructive), which obviously doesn't work with mesmerists and stalwarts having their own sets of Facets. I'm thinking that mesmerists should use Cognitive instead for theirs, and stalwarts should use Forceful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T10:30:54-07:00","id":1444676,"title":"","content":"I totally agree with all the changes. That is something would make them far more related to their more powerful counterparts.<br /> <br /> We were discussing DE by non talents, and I agree that it should be open to all the characters, DE should be completely meta-gaming, like gaining and spending momentum, and be available to all player characters (including Novas and Psions), not as a character power but as a player tool. BUT it should cost more than just 1 Momentum, probably 2 momentum for every inspiration.<br /> <br /> One option that may be interesting is use twists of Fate from Scion, you don\u2019t spend momentum, but you have a number of uses related to you path dots, and the DE is limited to something related to the used path (a military character could find an weapon or discover the adversary henchman is an old friend from their serving time, while a detective could find some clue or have a contact that know exactly what is needed to solve the problem).<br /> <br /> In Adventure d20 they brought the idea of special Feats that you could gain if you have enough levels in a class, making it easier/possible to DE almost the entire scene when it\u2019s relevant to the archetype (in the Storypath it would be related to the path). Something to think about at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 04-19-2021, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T11:33:47-07:00","id":1444690,"title":"","content":"Thinking more about it (after eating with that in mind), I think the idea of importing Twists of Fate from Scion, and allowing Talents to use inspiration to gain extra uses (and/or more powerful ones) is the best way to give DE to all characters.<br /> <br /> It fits even the effects many characters have in super heroes (like the character not dying, or the help arriving at the right time) while keeping the uses of some Edges and Powers that give some limited DE to non talents.<br /> <br /> It would also give some advantage to characters that spend their XP in mundane stuff (read path rank) that is very much abandoned by Novas and Psions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}